<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="345714a3-e403-4388-8cba-619008e75b6f" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerSampleDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">

    <introduction>
      <para> The ApplicationTaskConsole project shows how the DemiCode Scheduler <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Tasks.ApplicationTask</codeEntityReference> is implemented. 
               The sample also shows how a task is configured to execute with a schedule.</para>
    </introduction>

   
                                    
    
        
            
            
            
<section>
  <title>Prerequisites</title>
  <content>
    <para>Navigate to the <legacyBold>DemiCode Scheduler 1.1\Samples</legacyBold> folder. Unzip the <legacyBold>SchedulerSamples.zip</legacyBold>
                    in the Samples folder.</para>
  </content>
</section>

            
               
            
            
<section>
  <title>To build the sample using the Command Prompt</title>
  <content>
    <list class="ordered">
                    <listItem>
                        <para>
                            Open the Visual Studio 2005 Command Prompt window and navigate to the <legacyBold>DemiCode Scheduler
                                1.1\Samples</legacyBold> folder.</para>
                    </listItem>
                    <listItem>
                        <para>
                            Type <legacyBold>msbuild ApplicationTaskConsole.sln</legacyBold> at the command line.</para>
                    </listItem>
                </list>
  </content>
</section>

            
                
            
            
<section>
  <title>To build the sample using Visual Studio</title>
  <content>
     <list class="ordered">
                    <listItem>
                        <para>
                            Open Windows Explorer and navigate to the <legacyBold>DemiCode Scheduler 1.1\Samples</legacyBold>
                            folder.</para>
                    </listItem>
                    <listItem>
                        <para>
                            Double-click the <legacyBold>ApplicationTaskConsole.sln</legacyBold> to open the file in Visual Studio.</para>
                    </listItem>
                    <listItem>
                        <para>
                            In the <legacyBold>Build</legacyBold> menu, select <legacyBold>Build Solution</legacyBold>.</para>
                    </listItem>
                </list>
  </content>
</section>

             
<section>
  <title>To run the sample</title>
  <content>
    <definitionTable>
                    <definition>
                        Follow these steps to run the sample console application:
                        <list class="ordered">
                            <listItem>Open a Command Prompt and navigate to the directory that contains the new
                                executable. <para/>
                                This will usually be <legacyBold>Samples\ApplicationTaskConsole\bin\Debug</legacyBold></listItem>
                            <listItem>Run the application by typing:
                            <code language="other">
                            ApplicationTaskConsole.exe [Enter]
                            </code>
                            </listItem>
                            <listItem>Let the application run for at least 10 seconds before pressing [ENTER]. Logging information from the scheduler should appear in the console 
                           and additional consoles are opened by the ApplicationTask .</listItem>
                        </list>
                    </definition>
                </definitionTable>
  </content>
</section>

            
                
            
            
<section>
  <title>Requirements</title>
  <content>
    <para>DemiCode Scheduler 1.1 and .NET Framework 2.0.</para>
  </content>
</section>

            
                
            
            
<section>
  <title>Remarks</title>
  <content>
    <definitionTable>
                    <definition>
                        This sample demonstrates how to implement the <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Tasks.ITask</codeEntityReference> interface. The source code 
                        for <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Tasks.ApplicationTask</codeEntityReference> is included in the sample but not shown here for brevity.
                    </definition>
                    <definition>
                        With a few lines of code we create a simple console application. 
                        <code language="c#">
static void Main()
{
    // 1. Create default scheduler from configuration
    using (Scheduler _scheduler = SchedulerFactory.CreateFromConfig("scheduling"))
    {
        // 2. Start the engine
        _scheduler.Start();

        // 3. Wait for user input
        Console.WriteLine("Press [ENTER] to exit");
        Console.ReadLine();

        // 4. Stop the engine
        _scheduler.Stop();
    }
}                        </code>
                    </definition>
                    <definition>
                        The configuration contains our task, a logger and a schedule. In this sample we use the ConsoleLogger to output information to our console window.
                        <code language="xml">
&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-16" ?&gt;
&lt;configuration&gt;
    &lt;configSections&gt;
        &lt;section name=&quot;scheduling&quot; type=&quot;DemiCode.Scheduling.Configuration.SchedulerSettings, DemiCode.Scheduling, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=069d10bcdee4c3e4&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/configSections&gt;

    &lt;scheduling defaultScheduler=&quot;prod&quot;&gt;
        &lt;schedulers&gt;
            &lt;scheduler name=&quot;prod&quot;&gt;
                &lt;tasks&gt;
                    &lt;task type=&quot;ApplicationTaskConsole.Tasks.ApplicationTask, ApplicationTaskConsole&quot;
                        path=&quot;cmd&quot; arguments=&quot;/K &amp;quot;echo Application executed&quot; /&gt;
                &lt;/tasks&gt;
                &lt;loggers&gt;
                    &lt;ConsoleLogger /&gt;
                &lt;/loggers&gt;
                &lt;IntervalSchedule name=&quot;interval&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;start&gt;2006-11-30 15:50:00&lt;/start&gt;
                    &lt;interval&gt;00:00:10&lt;/interval&gt;
                &lt;/IntervalSchedule&gt;
            &lt;/scheduler&gt;
        &lt;/schedulers&gt;
    &lt;/scheduling&gt;
&lt;/configuration&gt;
</code>
                    
                    </definition>
                </definitionTable>
  </content>
</section>

            
                
            
               
        
    

